    "data": "Recent preprints evaluate deep‑learning antibody‑antigen modeling. B‑cell epitope restraints (BepiPocket, DiscoPocket) boost Chai‑1 predictions. AlphaFold3 outperforms AlphaFold2, Boltz‑1 and Chai‑1 but struggles with low co‑evolution targets; sampling improves success modestly. A depth‑over‑pairing principle shows MSA depth matters more than pairing. ABAG‑Rank learns to rank AlphaFold ensembles, surpassing internal scores. FoldBench reveals >50% failure on Ab‑Ag cases; AlphaFold3 remains top performer. POISK (89k patent‑derived records) shows folding models can enrich binders (72% pairwise accuracy) but miss epitope localization. EnsPlex combines multiple generators and FACET ranking, gaining up to 27.8% success on 102 Ab‑Ag systems. Boltz‑2 confidence metrics weakly discriminate binders (ROC‑AUC <0.60). Geometry‑over‑coevolution analysis indicates monomer geometry drives complex assembly, explaining Ab‑Ag difficulty. IntelliFold‑2 surpasses AlphaFold3 on therapeutic settings. AF2Dock adapts co‑folding for structure‑based docking, offering orthogonal predictions. Cryo‑EM resolves a 3 Å Fab 37E5–MLC1 peptide complex, detailing antigen recognition.",
